# KB viva del profilo: caricamento completo. Le precedenti misure con KB
# ridotta sono obsolete; le attese legacy richiedono rivalidazione semantica.
# migrated from tests/cases/analogy.chat (gen346, hermetic + isolated)
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test analogy]
# gen102 (L11): structural analogy "A is to B as C is to ?". The answer is NOT
# stored anywhere — it is DERIVED from a binary relation the KB holds. The
# relations are taught in ordinary form ("X is the capital of Y" -> capital(X,Y));
# the analogy then transfers to a held-out pair the system was never given.

# gen506: «X is the capital of Y» e «the capital of Y is X» finiscono nello
# STESSO cassetto (`capital_of/2`, via `relation_noun/2`), e la ricevuta e' prosa.
# 28 settembre 2026: con il ponte `predicate_reverse_of(capital_of,
# capital_of_country)` (parrot-p0-syntax.md §19) le capitali del mondo sono gia'
# `capital_of`: la lezione e' tenuta, non nuova, e la ricevuta lo dice.
> rome is the capital of italy
<~ the capital of italy is rome
> paris is the capital of france
<~ the capital of france is paris

# Forward: find capital(rome, italy), then resolve capital(paris, ?) -> france.
> rome is to italy as paris is to what?
< france.
# The proof is real — it cites the two relations the analogy stands on.
> how do you know?
# La relazione scelta e' una di quelle che valgono per entrambe le coppie
# (`capital_of` o `located_in`, dalla KB viva): la prova le cita davvero.
<~ holds, and
<~ so france.

# Reverse direction: the SAME relation read the other way. italy:rome :: france:?
# resolves capital(?, france) -> paris. Structural, not a memorized pair.
> italy is to rome as france is to what?
< paris.

# Honest miss: the analogy SHAPE is recognized, the relation is found, but the
# fourth term is unknown — say exactly that instead of guessing or echoing.
# 28 settembre 2026: Berlino ora e' nota (il ponte porta il cassetto del mondo),
# «germany» e' la risposta vera; il mancato onesto si prova su un nome ignoto.
> rome is to italy as berlin is to what?
<~ germany
> rome is to italy as zorbak is to what?
# gen506: il ramo «relazione trovata, quarto termine ignoto» non metteva il
# messaggio nella risposta e il turno usciva con l'eco del turno prima; ora
# parla, e la resa presenta i nomi propri e la relazione senza underscore.
<~ but I don't know that relation for Zorbak.
